#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059664 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059495 :question/id #uuid "652143ae-b765-5abe-a7e9-a90ec15dd38f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3521" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $\\tan \\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12} \\right)$.\n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $$\n\\displaystyle \\dfrac{\\pi}{12} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} - \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}.\n$$*" :question/worked-solution "Recall the difference formula for tangent:\n\n$$\n\\tan(x-y) = \\dfrac{\\tan{x}-\\tan{y}}{1+\\tan{x}\\tan{y}}\n$$\n\nApplying the difference formula for tangent with\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan \\left(\\frac{π}{12}\\right) &= \\tan (\\frac{π}{3} - \\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n&= (\\tan \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right) - \\tan \\left(\\frac{π}{4}\\right))/(1 + \\tan \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)\\tan \\left(\\frac{π}{4}\\right)) \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{1 + \\sqrt{3} \\cdot 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we rationalize the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan \\left(\\frac{π}{12}\\right) &= \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{\\sqrt{3} + 1} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3} - 1}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} \\\\\n&= ((\\sqrt{3})^{2} - 2\\sqrt{3} + (-1)^{2})/((\\sqrt{3})^{2} - 1^{2}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{3 - 2\\sqrt{3} + 1}{3 - 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4 - 2\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\\n&= 2 - \\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b97e00a-b343-5b04-b475-3aaa038995ca" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048229 :topic/id #uuid "8a462f76-1e1a-5c54-833e-8d3d6162407f" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054757} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054758} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054759}] :topic/math-academy-id 86 :topic/next [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048758} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050180}] :topic/title "Rationalizing Denominators With Two Terms"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049847 :topic/id #uuid